{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/importance.ts@L15","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/importance.ts","span":{"start":15,"end":16}},"file":"packages/core/src/importance.ts","span":{"start":15,"end":16},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:e04dac5a37faf36094b433ceb00daddfcbd5794d98873dec508b91309b897601","meta":{"text":"A symbol's derived kind — the architectural subtype the viz renders and ranking weights by.\n`NodeKind` widened with the derived symbol kinds `deriveNodeKind` resolves a raw `symbol` into."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/importance.ts@L64","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/importance.ts","span":{"start":64,"end":64}},"file":"packages/core/src/importance.ts","span":{"start":64,"end":64},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:722cd7679b85d30fb587a3074dcc759d25002f4e1587ba75405d3a1118d7ef09","meta":{"text":"Resolve a raw `symbol` node into its architectural subtype; non-symbol kinds pass through."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/importance.ts@L80","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/importance.ts","span":{"start":80,"end":81}},"file":"packages/core/src/importance.ts","span":{"start":80,"end":81},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:214e1510af6648cd2cb18433a3cdb946584294c4142c30a2695dcc3c5507949b","meta":{"text":"A baseline importance floor for structural container kinds, so a file/class/interface/route/\ntable still ranks above the noise floor even with zero incoming architectural edges."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/importance.ts@L96","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/importance.ts","span":{"start":96,"end":101}},"file":"packages/core/src/importance.ts","span":{"start":96,"end":101},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:1719c3b99ec07311d7ea742f328810ca732b722861e236dafe4abb233fe2397e","meta":{"text":"Compute per-node importance over the whole soul: directed in-degree over ARCHITECTURAL_RELS,\ndecorated by `kindBase` and a 0.1 noise-kind weight. Returns a Map keyed by node id. Only nodes\nwith an incoming architectural edge OR a non-zero kindBase appear (leaf symbols with no callers\nand no base bump carry importance 0 and are intentionally absent — callers use `?? 0`)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/enums.ts@L146","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":146,"end":147}},"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":146,"end":147},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:df9318b808d2649493d698801af0b30f537528957afd5fa3cee16804b14184cb","meta":{"text":"Who executed the gate. `cli` and `ci` produce trusted receipts; `mcp` never executes (PRD: \"Do\nnot execute commands or models through MCP\")."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/enums.ts@L23","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":23,"end":23}},"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":23,"end":23},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:5b7cf4d9a6976e9a0c77717348b8c29e490c65d1c2bda9b9b7a4493dff4802de","meta":{"text":"Trust axis: where the claim is admitted. `candidate` = untrusted staging, never in normal recall."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/enums.ts@L28","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":28,"end":28}},"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":28,"end":28},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:720d11c33d09aadf0740147728ff6bc16bad388816af8220203bf6b506bc7c28","meta":{"text":"Evidence axis: whether the claim's evidence survives admissibility + revalidation."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/enums.ts@L33","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":33,"end":33}},"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":33,"end":33},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:ba16fc4b51c95fd3781fc6d4db77a56431fc3e8bc4f028c861eea821ea825f1a","meta":{"text":"Applicability axis: whether the claim still attaches to a live code/doc target."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/enums.ts@L42","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":42,"end":42}},"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":42,"end":42},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:606516694fb927fdb89e665bc22c12cb2180fbf97c2fc00d524eb5f3374af579","meta":{"text":"Lifecycle axis: whether the claim has been retired by a decision event."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/enums.ts@L51","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":51,"end":52}},"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":51,"end":52},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:7a9290ca594cb50b7acd4430ba6defa5b434c33460f516173426a20b1814fc5c","meta":{"text":"The four verdicts stamped on a record (as-of save/last-evaluation). The READ PROJECTION overlays\ndecision events + freshness revalidation to compute the effective verdicts (Slice 3)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/enums.ts@L75","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":75,"end":87}},"file":"packages/memory/src/enums.ts","span":{"start":75,"end":87},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:7c92ed87c5d3f31f2a181738c53d086fba536eb3d2b97642ff3fbe8684ddaeee","meta":{"text":"The admissible evidence kinds, one per `MemoryEvidence` item. Each is checked INDEPENDENTLY\n(PRD: \"every claim is checked independently\"). An agent assertion is never evidence (PRD), so\nthere is no `agent-assertion` kind.\n- `source-quote`        — a verified quote from a committed source span (Fact / Procedure).\n- `execution-assertion` — an allowlisted assertion from a sanitized GateReceipt (Fact / Procedure).\n- `committed-policy`    — a reference to a tracked agent-artifact (instruction/rule/skill) anchor (Procedure / Decision / Convention).\n- `human-attestation`   — a human TTY attestation (Decision / Convention / Pitfall reproduction).\n- `receipt-pair`        — a failing receipt plus a subsequent passing receipt (Pitfall).\n`receipt-pair` and `reproduction` (source-quote + human-attestation) compose the Pitfall evidence."}}
